 birth he had never before seen men and women, or any other creatures living in cities and towns.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-10-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1009009","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0192105fe4078682d1822b0b4ec6ce4a287789641bde7d091749552bcc99ec01","compact":"48f2eb3768cc0e954c62a7e3c31c98338128ff8a84546702040f50ee6e90be9c","nasal":"48f2eb3768cc0e954c62a7e3c31c98338128ff8a84546702040f50ee6e90be9c"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-9-10","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":9,"verse":10,"english":"It came to pass that on one occasion, walking about at will, Vibhandaka's son came to that spot and beheld the courtezans.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.867,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-10-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1009010","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"179c5df393388894d56ca29afe77b657ae7e377355de55f3af24d6404675402f","compact":"9abc97b9b984de3e58d8d37227f92a0314b4d0b9bbd65b65bc85b42f7cd9a833","nasal":"9b40840e2ac8c18efd25ebe6d2739440774309ccef5729e2d59521af50e2a7dc"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-9-11","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":9,"verse":11,"english":"Colourfully attired, and singing sweet songs, the women came to the saint's son and said.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.859,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-10-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1009011","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6da9b72c0ef30246d502e896b4c47d0b1e6f8bbc98bfbae3c3916f59db352b80","compact":"dd3e11bd19e7aecd8517a630775c48c7f182599791f5b4c66660c8a6ee6b802c","nasal":"1250ef2047bffff69df45fa33562fa55362cbaf9d1ef6e3f9df1538710956e72"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-9-12","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":9,"verse":12,"english":"Who are you? And where are you going, O Brahman? We wish to learn all this. And why is it that you range alone this far-off forest?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.723,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-10-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1009012","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4f39366be27c59ebd42bedbdbb6b9ef885c31c4297eea252d92337eb26cd7775","compact":"eb7f4a03f7865e5357f120ce9657a332d95ca7de3a96ea76d73c23d37bdaba63","nasal":"4bebb1d825510a495946d82bfc8ad2d77e1c320919e417c76e07ff7c90aafd8f"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-9-13","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":9,"verse":13,"english":"Beholding these beautiful damsels never seen before, he from delight, hastened to inform them of his lineage.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-10-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1009013","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"24d06c7e9f187776e8833f64655d5df0dfbd5beb9db4535abdbfb1bf777faf28","compact":"3ae9ff12011227bf4b7b6bb2bf0bd66e0a0c22794c44826f3dc4ac0333cfb5d3","nasal":"3ae9ff12011227bf4b7b6bb2bf0bd66e0a0c22794c44826f3dc4ac0333cfb5d3"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-9-14","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":9,"verse":14,"english":"My father is Vibhăndaka; and I am his son. My name is Rşyasſiga and my occupation is known the world over.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.862,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-10-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1009014","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5cc577ba6cab4d7ad26a49dceef15e2bb766373ee1d761a8e1186fa9bf47c44a","compact":"c7f94254f563716f0875b0af2fdedb59037ddeb7dd3ca89bdb9c73c4dcecea2a","nasal":"d8990a6ca6782767c286cac0eb6003e0648052310ec680ce091039eaefb6de30"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-9-15","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":9,"verse":15,"english":"This auspicious hermitage hard by belongs to us; and there I shall receive you all in due form O' lovely ones! .","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-10-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1009015","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2c41b12148dcefb66f9d40316decf7f5432a671e9f1fa5c2fc7ec080cc229138","compact":"c4d4581a6f0e6c6cfeae477582165b27de45f477c44c2a0a5e7653bb33b75ebe","nasal":"c4d4581a6f0e6c6cfeae477582165b27de45f477c44c2a0a5e7653bb33b75ebe"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-9-16","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":9,"verse":16,"english":"Hearing the words of the saint's son, they all consented, and the women went to behold that asylum.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.891,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-10-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1009016","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b75a98122973e74bfe482d0bad21992a9541a2fffa2b350d8d41693413c220a4","compact":"ea2e499a633a20e35d344b46418b42e8bef90adfb600a3ae4101e27aec2e11fa","nasal":"ea2e499a633a20e35d344b46418b42e8bef90adfb600a3ae4101e27aec2e11fa"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-9-17","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":9,"verse":17,"english":"When they had come there, the saint's son received them hospitably, saying, 'Here is Arghya,' 'Here is water for washing the feet,' 'Here are fruits and roots.'","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.855,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-10-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1009017","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0e8bcdfca29cf3c6524366ecc70de92d586918f70bff7ce775a2463a1b2640ff","compact":"a64794030022aee254dbf7e5ec9cc835ce5b10caa614c366296aa7af3927665d","nasal":"a64794030022aee254